### Problem

Zotero MCP works great for analyzing individual papers interactively, but systematic literature reviews require applying the same analysis to dozens or even hunderds of papers. Currently, this means either:

1. Manually asking the same question about each paper through conversation
2. Building external scripts that lose Zotero MCP's benefits

### Proposed Solution
Add basic batch processing to apply the same query to multiple papers:

```javascript
zotero_batch_query({
  query: "Extract methodology, key findings, and limitations from this paper",
  collection: "Climate Policy Papers",
  max_concurrent: 3
})
// Returns: batch_id
```

```javascript
zotero_get_batch_results(batch_id)
// Returns: [
//   {
//     item_id: "ABC123",
//     title: "Paper Title", 
//     response: "Methodology: Survey of 500 participants...",
//     error: null
//   }
// ]
```

